  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale  \n   We use a genetic algorithm to minimize the overlap integral C5 by evolving binary sequences that satisfy the integral constraint and inherent function properties. The method starts from the parent solution and explores local variations while maintaining feasibility. The search space is structured to represent the function h(x) as a step function optimized for minimal maximum overlap with its shifts.  \n\n2. Mathematical specification  \n   - Representation: h is represented as a binary sequence of length n = 45 (or multiples) with sum S = n/2.  \n   - Objective: C5 = max_k (2/n) * |np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full')|  \n   - Constraints:  \n      0 <= h[i] <= 1 for all i  \n      sum(h) = n/2  \n   - Repair: After mutation/crossover, clip values to [0,1] and adjust sum via minimal redistribution.  \n\n3. Implementation procedure  \n   - Initialization: Start with parent_solution (45-point array) with necessary mutations. Handles n=45 base case.  \n   - Feasibility repair: Clip to [0,1] then adjust sum by:  \n     \u2022 Sort values, modify smallest/largest to meet sum requirement  \n   - Objective evaluation: Direct computation using np.correlate  \n   - Operators: Crossover over blocks (max 15) and point mutations  \n   - Early termination: Monotonic improvement observed  \n   - Population: Dynamic list storing best 50 candidates  \n\n4. Search choices and variations  \n   - Base grid: n = 45 (explicitly uses parent solution)  \n   - Population size: 400  \n   - Mutation probability: 0.8  \n   - Crossover probability: 0.4  \n   - Reduction grid: Not used (parent solution fixed)  \n   - Feasibility repair chance: 0.8  \n   - Minimum check period: 100 generations  \n\n5. Compute budget and robustness  \n   - Estimating time: n=45, 1000 fitness evaluations/second \u2192 45 seconds  \n   - Fallback mechanism: If candidate improves, replace current best  \n   - NaN handling: Repair until numerical stability  \n\n6. Validation and return contract  \n   - Final fitness check: np.isfinite(correlation) and result < 0.38085  \n   - Return tuple: (best_h_array, C5_value, 45)  \n   - Repair ensures: 0 <= h[i] <= 1 and |sum(h) - 45/2| < 1e-5",
